\par Q AND YOU DON'T HAVE SPECIFIC KNOWLEDGE AS TO HOW TO DELETE THE FOOTPRINTS THAT WE HAVE JUST MADE REFERENCE TO ON THE C.D.'S, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A NO. 
\par Q WHEN YOU SAY NO, YOU AGREE, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. I WOULDN'T KNOW HOW TO DO THAT. 
\par Q HAVE YOU EVER READ -- IS THAT SOMETHING THAT I COULD MAYBE FIND IN "COMPUTER EDGE"? DO YOU KNOW WHAT "COMPUTER EDGE" IS? 
\par A THE ONLY WAY THAT I WOULD KNOW TO FIGURE OUT HOW TO DO THAT WOULD BE TO DO IT AND TRY AND LOOK AT IT AGAIN WITH THE FORENSICS TOOL AND SEE IF THAT WORKED. 
\par Q DID YOU NOTICE ANY EVIDENCE IN -- ON ANY OF THE MEDIA OF THE EXISTENCE OF A FORENSICS TOOL DESIGNED TO DELETE FOOTPRINTS? MR. CLARKE: OBJECTION. LACK OF FOUNDATION. THE COURT: OVERRULED. YOU CAN ANSWER. THE WITNESS: NO. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q MR. CLARKE ASKED YOU WHETHER OR NOT ALL OF THESE PICTURES COULD HAVE BEEN VIEWED ON FEBRUARY THE 1ST, 2002. THEY COULD HAVE BEEN VIEWED ANY TIME SINCE THEIR CREATION, ISN'T THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S RIGHT. 
\par Q AND ANY OPINION YOU HAD WOULD REALLY BE JUST SPECULATIVE. 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q IN THE ABSENCE OF SOMETHING ON ONE OF YOUR FORENSICS PROGRAMS THAT WOULD GIVE THE DATE OF -- 
\par A IF I FOUND A LINK FILE IN ONE OF THE COMPUTERS THAT MATCHED A FILE NAME ON ONE OF THE LOOSE PIECES OF MEDIA, YOU WOULD HAVE A MORE REASONABLE BASIS FOR ASSUMING THAT PARTICULAR PICTURE HAD BEEN VIEWED. 
\par Q DO YOU KNOW WHETHER NEAL WESTERFIELD KNOWS HIS FATHER'S SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER? 
\par A I DON'T KNOW IF HE DOES OR NOT. 
\par Q DO YOU THINK THAT IF -- IS THERE A FORENSIC REASON WHY THE OWNER OF A COMPUTER THAT PRESUMABLY IS HIS PERSONAL COMPUTER WOULD US
E HIS SON'S E-MAIL TO SIGN ONTO THE COMPUTER IN ANY MANNER? MR. CLARKE: OBJECTION. CALLS FOR SPECULATION. THE COURT: SUSTAINED. YOU NEED NOT ANSWER. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q CAN YOU THINK OF ANY REASON WHY THE OWNER OF A PERSONAL COMPUTER WOULD USE ANOTHER PERSO
N'S NAME TO SIGN ON WHERE THAT INDIVIDUAL HAS UNIQUE AND UNRESTRICTED INDIVIDUAL ACCESS? MR. CLARKE: SAME OBJECTION. THE COURT: SAME RULING. YOU NEED NOT ANSWER, SIR. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q YOU TALKED ABOUT REPORTS THAT YOU READ FROM THE REGIONAL COMPUTER FORENSICS LAB. ONE OF THOSE REPORTS WAS PREPARED BY A MAN NAMED ARMSTRONG, ISN'T THAT RIGHT? 
\par A I BELIEVE SO, YES. 
\par Q AND YOU TOOK INTO CONSIDERATION IN EVALUATING YOUR CONCLUSIONS THAT THE SAN DIEGO REGIONAL COMPUTER FORENSICS LAB. CONCLUDED -- MR. CLARKE: OBJECTION. CALLS FOR HEARSAY. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
