\par Q WITH REGARD TO THE HARD DRIVE THAT YOU WERE EVALUATING, YOU WERE ASKED QUESTIONS BY MR. CLARKE ABOUT LOOSE MEDIA AND DID YOU ASK FOR THIS MEDIA OR THAT MEDIA. THE EN CASE SOFTWARE REQUIRES YOU TO UTILIZE HARD DRIVES, DOES IT? 
\par A NO. IT DOESN'T REQUIRE YOU TO USE HARD DRIVES. 
\par Q WELL, WAS THERE A PROBLEM IN YOU USING C.D.'S AND ZIP DISKS INSTEAD OF HAVING THE DATA TRANSFERRED TO A HARD DRIVE? 
\par A NO. 
\par Q WHY DID YOU ASK FOR IT TO BE TRANSFERRED TO A HARD DRIVE? 
\par A I DON'T RECALL THAT I DID. 
\par Q OKAY. ULTIMATELY WHAT DID YOU END UP WITH FOR PURPOSES OF YOUR FORENSIC EVALUATION? WHAT I'M ASKING YOU, WHAT I'M REALLY TRYING TO ASK YOU IS HOW MUCH DATA DID YOU HAVE. DID YOU HAVE A NUMBER OF HARD DRIVES; DID YOU HAVE SOME C.D.'S? WHAT
 DID YOU HAVE; WHAT WERE YOU LOOKING AT? 
\par A THERE WERE A TOTAL OF SIX HARD DRIVES THAT WERE PRESENTED TO ME. 
\par Q OKAY. I WANT YOU TO TELL ME. 
\par A IN ONE OF THOSE HARD DRIVES CONTAINED INDIVIDUAL COPIES OF THE INIVIDUAL PIECES OF LOOSE MEDIA COPIED TO ONE HARD DRIVE. 
\par Q DID THAT PROCESS IN ANY MANNER AFFECT YOUR ABILITY TO RECONSTRUCT DATES OF ACCESS OR ANY OF THAT? 
\par A YES. 
\par Q HOW SO? 
\par A WHEN C.D.'S ARE COPIED TO A HARD DRIVE SUCH AS THAT, IT WILL CHANGE THE DATES OF THE -- OF SOME OF THE SUBFOLDERS AND FOLDERS ON THE C.D. TO THE CURRENT DATE THAT THE C.D. IS BEING COPIED. 
\par Q IN OTHER WORDS, IF I HAVE A C.D. BURNER AND I CREATE AND I TRY AND BURN A C.D., WHAT I'M GOING TO GET IS THE DATE I CREATE IT, IS THAT WHAT YOU'RE SAYING? 
\par A ON MANY OF THE FOLDERS AND SUBFOLDERS. THAT'S NOT TRUE OF ALL OF THE DATES OF ALL OF THE FILES ON THE MEDIA, BUT MANY OF THE FOLDERS WILL ASSUME THE DATE OF THE DATE THE C.D. IS BEING COPIED. 
\par Q SO, IN OTHER WORDS, HAD YOU GOTTEN A COPY OF THE C.D.'S, THE DATES WOULDN'T HAVE BEEN I GUESS APPROPRIATE FOR THE KIND OF INVESTIGATION YOU NEEDED TO DO. 
\par A I'M SORRY. COULD YOU ASK ME THAT AGAIN? 
\par Q SURE. IF YOU HAD GONE TO EITHER THROUGH MY OFFICE OR DIRECTLY TO MR. WATKINS OR THE R. C. F. L. AND SAID YOU WANTED A COPY OF THE C.D., A C.D., AND
 THEY DID A STANDARD DISK COPY OR WHATEVER IT'S CALLED, WOULD THE COPY OF THE C.D. THAT RESULTED IN ANY WAY AFFECT YOUR ABILITY TO RECONSTRUCT THE ORIGINAL DATA? 
\par A YOU WOULD HAVE TO USE A FORENSIC SOFTWARE TO DO SO. YOU CAN'T JUST COPY IT FROM ONE C.D. TO ANOTHER. YOU HAVE TO USE A NORTON GHOST OR EN CASE AND MAKE YOUR COPY. 
\par Q I'M SORRY. DID YOU MAKE IT APPARENT THAT AT LEAST FROM THE SAN DIEGO LAB. YOU WANTED THE HARD DRIVES TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH EN CASE SOFTWARE SO THAT YOU COULD UTILIZE THAT FORENSIC TOOL? 
\par A YES. 
\par Q WITH REGARDS TO THE ISSUE OF LABELING A C.D., WE'VE LEARNED THERE'S A PROGRAM CALLED ADAPTEK. HAVE YOU EVER HEARD OF ADAPTEK? 
\par A YES. 
\par Q THAT'S A PROGRAM THAT ALLOWS YOU TO CREATE A C.D. THAT YOU CAN BOTH READ AND WRITE, IS THAT CORRECT? 
\par A THE C.D. ITSELF ALSO HAS TO BE A READ/WRITE C.D., BUT YES. 
\par Q SO IF I USE ADAPTEK SOFTWARE, CAN I CREATE A LABEL TO SAY ANYTHING I WANT IT TO SAY? 
\par A I THINK THAT YOU CAN, BUT I'M NOT SURE. 
\par Q WELL, YOU CREATE C.D.'S FROM TIME TO TIME, DON'T YOU? 
\par A YES. 
\par Q THERE'S A COMMAND AS YOU ARE CREATING A C.D. THAT ASKS YOU TO NAME IT, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q I DON'T KNOW. IS THAT CALLED A VOLUME? 
\par A I'M NOT SURE WHAT IT'S CALLED SPECIFICALLY. TECHNICALLY I'M NOT SURE WHAT IT'S CALLED. 
\par Q ONCE THE C.D.'S NAMED, THE NAME STAYS FOREVER, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q BUT THE NAME DOESN'T COME WITH THE COMPUTER, IT COMES WITH THE PERSON THAT'S CREATING THE C.D., ISN'T THAT TRUE? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q SO THAT MEANS THAT I COULD TAKE THIS LAPTOP COMPUTER IF IT HAD A C.D. BURNER AND CREATE ONE DISK, ONE C.D. DISK THAT SAID, HYPOTHETICALLY, SPECTRUM DESIGN, RIGHT? 
\par A CORRECT. 
\par Q AND YOU WOULD NEVER KNOW WHETHER IT WAS DAVID WESTERFIELD'S SPECTRUM DESIGN OR STEVE FELDMAN'S RIPPING HIM OFF. MR. CLARKE: OBJE
CTION. THE WITNESS: YES. MR. CLARKE: CALLS FOR SPECULATION. THE COURT: SUSTAINED. MR. CLARKE: MOVE TO STRIKE THE ANSWER. THE COURT: THE JURY IS TO DISREGARD THE ANSWER. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q IT IS IMPOSSIBLE TO TELL MERELY ON THE BASIS OF THE NAME ON THE C.D. WHO THE CREATOR OF THE C.D. IS. 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q YOU MIGHT WANT SOME OTHER FORENSIC DEVICES TO HELP YOU SUCH AS FINGERPRINTS, RIGHT? MR. CLARKE: OBJECTION. I THINK THIS IS BEYOND THE SCOPE. THE COURT: SUSTAINED. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q WE DIDN'T ASK YOU OR DID WE HAVE CONVERSATIONS ABOUT YOU PRINTING UP EVERY SINGLE SCREEN PRINT THAT -- EVERY SINGLE SCREEN PRINT, A COPY OF EVERY SINGLE SCREEN? DID WE EVER TALK ABOUT THAT? 
\par A NO. YOU WANT TO MAKE THE DISTINCTION BETWEEN EVERY SINGLE SCREEN PRINT AND EVERY SINGLE SCREEN. 
\par Q YES. 
\par A BECAUSE YOU HAVE SEEN, AS FAR AS I AM AWARE, YOU HAVE SEEN EVERY SCREEN PRINT THAT I HAVE MADE IN THIS CASE. CERTAINLY NOT EVERY SCREEN I'VE LOOKED AT. I'VE LOOKED AT THOUSANDS AND THOUSANDS OF SCREENS. SO. . . 
\par Q WHAT'S INVOLVED IN MAKING A SCREEN PRINT? YOU PUT TOGETHER THE BINDER THAT WE'VE HAD MARKED -- I'M SORRY -- IF YOU LOOK ON THE OUTSIDE, IT GIVES US AN EXHIBIT NUMBER. THE COURT: 157. MR. FELDMAN: THANK YOU. BY MR. FELDMAN: 
\par Q -- WE HAVE HAD MARKED 157, AND IT HAS A SERIES OF SCREEN PRINTS, SIR. WHAT DOES IT TAKE TO CREATE ONE OF THOSE? HOW DOES THAT HAPPEN? 
\par A THE SCREEN PRINT PROGRAM RUNS IN THE BACKGROUND OF MY INVESTIGATIVE MACHINE. AND WHEN I AM VIEWING SOMETHING ON THE SCREEN THAT I WANT TO CAPTURE FOR LATER REPORT OR WHATEVER, I HIT PRINT SCREEN BUTTON. 
\par Q HOW LONG DOES IT TAKE? 
\par A I'M EMBARRASSED TO SAY, BUT OUR PRINTERS ARE FAIRLY SLOW. WE DON'T HAVE ANY COLOR LASER PRINTERS ATTACHED TO OUR FORENSIC MACHINES. THEY ARE ALL INK JET PRINTERS. AND IT TAKES A MINUTE OR SO TO PRINT OUT ANY GIVEN SCREEN PRINT. 
\par Q AND IF THERE'S MORE DETAIL TO THE SCREENS, IT TAKES LONGER? 
\par A IT TAKES LONGER, THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q AND IF THERE'S BIGGER PICTURES, IT TAKES LONGER THAN IF THERE IS JUST LANGUAGE ACROSS, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. 
\par Q SO THE MORE DETAIL IN THE PARTICULAR SCREEN PRINT, THE LONGER IT TAKES TO PRINT, IS THAT RIGHT? 
\par A THAT'S CORRECT. MR. FELDMAN: YOUR HONOR, JUST ONE MOMENT. THE COURT: SURE. (PAUSE.) BY MR. FELDMAN: 
